Subject: [PATCH 166/206] F37 erratum for b2e93350653: prog pool is 3849, not
 2779

b2e93350653's message states "prog 2779 (unchanged)". That number was
written before it was measured and is wrong. Measured on a private copy of
the oracle dir after rebuilding from b2e93350653:

  pool size  hello 1421/1421, prog 3849/3849, base_dd 1421/1421
             (ours/theirs, --dump_object_pool object_pool_size)
  at their `2312 (obj)` slots, ours now reads `3928 (obj)`
  (ProductSimARM64, hello 92, prog 178, base_dd 92) and `3968 (obj)`
  (ReleaseARM64, hello 92); before b2e93350653 these were
  `0x1eb0 (unknown)` / `0x1f00 (unknown)`.

The negative-control sentence in b2e93350653 was also written before the
control ran. It has since been run and holds: reverting only the emission
to AddImmediate (uncommitted) gives op_dump_check.sh rc=1, 1323/1421
identical, 92 slots `0x1f00 (unknown)` vs their `2312 (obj)`; restored and
rebuilt, 0 ninja pending in ProductSimARM64, ReleaseARM64, ProductARM64.

measure_dd_emission.sh exits 1 at both 63716223bde and b2e93350653 because
dd_emission.expected pins ours native_patched=0; the reading is ours 92,
theirs 92. That pin lives outside this tree and is not changed here.

An amend was refused by the non-fast-forward reference-transaction hook,
hence this separate commit.

